          ],
          "grounding_supports": [
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0,
                1
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": null,
                "end_index": 165,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "The destruction of over 100 works of contemporary and modern art in the May 2004 Momart warehouse fire in Leyton, East London, was far more than a financial disaster"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2,
                1
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 167,
                "end_index": 430,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "While the immediate economic toll was massive\u2014with losses estimated between \u00a330 million and \u00a350 million and a subsequent string of high-profile lawsuits and secret settlements\u2014the fire was, in reality, a profound cultural, philosophical, and emotional event"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                3,
                0
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 618,
                "end_index": 770,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "The Erasure of Cultural and Historical Milestones\nMany of the destroyed works belonged to Charles Saatchi\u2019s collection of Young British Artists (YBAs)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2,
                0
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 772,
                "end_index": 924,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "These were not just expensive commodities; they were the physical monuments of the 1990s \"Cool Britannia\" movement and the iconic *Sensation* exhibition"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                4,
                5
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 926,
                "end_index": 1029,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Works like Tracey Emin\u2019s *Everyone I Have Ever Slept With 1963\u20131995* (famously known as \"the tent\")"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2,
                1
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 926,
                "end_index": 1106,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Works like Tracey Emin\u2019s *Everyone I Have Ever Slept With 1963\u20131995* (famously known as \"the tent\") and Jake and Dinos Chapman's monumental, meticulously crafted diorama *Hell*"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                6,
                2
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1154,
                "end_index": 1342,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Furthermore, the fire also destroyed a massive portion of the life's work of recently deceased artists, such as the modernist abstract painter Patrick Heron and the sculptor Helen Chadwick"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                6
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1344,
                "end_index": 1538,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Because these artists were no longer alive, these works could never be remade, leading Heron\u2019s family to describe the event as a \"national artistic tragedy, a cultural loss on a massive scale\""
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1710,
                "end_index": 1975,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "** The differing responses from the artists themselves proved that art's value is deeply tied to its context and creation:\n* **Tracey Emin's Refusal:** Following the fire, Saatchi offered Emin \u00a31 million (funded by his insurance payout) to recreate her famous tent"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                5
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1977,
                "end_index": 1996,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Emin firmly refused"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                8,
                9
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1998,
                "end_index": 2112,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "She argued that the work was a physical time capsule of a specific chapter of her life that could not be simulated"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2114,
                "end_index": 2249,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "To Emin, recreating the tent would be \"morally wrong\" because it would lack the genuine \"emotional input\" of the original 1995 creation"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2401,
                "end_index": 2474,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Rather than mourn the loss of *Hell* (which took them two years to build)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                10
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2401,
                "end_index": 2505,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Rather than mourn the loss of *Hell* (which took them two years to build), they embraced the destruction"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                11,
                12
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2507,
                "end_index": 2593,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "In 2008, they unveiled *Fucking Hell*\u2014a new, even larger, and more grotesque version"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                10
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2595,
                "end_index": 2730,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "They explicitly stated they wanted to remake the piece to \"rescue the work from the sentimentality\" that had surrounded its destruction"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2,
                0
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2859,
                "end_index": 2989,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Initially, parts of the British tabloid media and traditionalist art critics reacted with blatant *schadenfreude* (malicious glee)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                7,
                0
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2991,
                "end_index": 3101,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Critics of the YBA movement mocked the event, joking that \"trash\" had simply been thrown back into the furnace"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3105,
                "end_index": 3323,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "It was only when the public realized that revered, traditional abstract works\u2014like those of Patrick Heron\u2014had also been turned to ash that the tone of the national conversation shifted from mockery to genuine grief"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3579,
                "end_index": 3626,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Many lost physical records of their own history"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                6
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3628,
                "end_index": 3792,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Damien Hirst, for example, lost not only his own paintings but also works by close friends like Sarah Lucas and Gary Hume that he had personally collected or traded"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                7,
                13
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 4068,
                "end_index": 4341,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "By reducing tangible cultural touchstones to ash, it permanently altered the legacies of several artists, redefined the boundaries of what makes an artwork \"authentic,\" and proved that some losses are entirely beyond the reach of insurance payouts and financial settlements"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            }
          ],
